---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"nsenter\")"
---
Run a program in different namespaces

Usage: nsenter [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]...

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...  Program and arguments to run

Options:
  -t, --target <TARGET>       Target process to get namespaces from
  -a, --all                   Enter all namespaces of the target process
  -m, --mount [<MOUNT>]       Enter mount namespace
  -u, --uts [<UTS>]           Enter UTS namespace
  -i, --ipc [<IPC>]           Enter IPC namespace
  -n, --net [<NET>]           Enter network namespace
  -p, --pid [<PID>]           Enter PID namespace
  -U, --user [<USER>]         Enter user namespace
  -C, --cgroup [<CGROUP>]     Enter cgroup namespace
  -T, --time [<TIME>]         Enter time namespace
  -F, --no-fork               Don't fork before exec (default is to fork when entering PID
                              namespace)
      --preserve-credentials  Don't modify UID/GID when entering user namespace
  -r, --root [<ROOT_DIR>]     Set root directory
  -w, --wd [<WORK_DIR>]       Set working directory
  -S, --setuid <SET_UID>      Set UID in entered namespace
  -G, --setgid <SET_GID>      Set GID in entered namespace
  -h, --help                  Print help
